# UI and API use application facades

Pages, modals, and API endpoints gather arguments, start a job or return `IResult`, and show the result. They call `IWorkspace*Operations` or Queries / `IWorkspaceGitChangesReadService`. They must not resolve `WorkspaceGitService`, orchestrators, or `IGitChangesAgentClient`.

Allowed leftovers until a later pass:

- `IWorkspacePageService` bag properties already injected on the page
- `WorkspaceBranchHandler` bulk helpers (`FetchBranchesForWorkspaceAsync`, checkout/create helpers)
- Interactive Sync-to-default dialogs on the Repositories page
- `IGitChangesAgentClient` for discard and diff only (commit, stage, and unstage go through `IWorkspaceGitChangesOperations`)

New user-initiated mutations belong on the matching facade (`IWorkspaceUpdateOperations`, `IWorkspaceSyncOperations`, `IWorkspaceFileOperations`, `IWorkspaceGitChangesOperations`, `IWorkspaceBranchOperations`, and so on). Do not add a page or endpoint call to `WorkspaceGitService` or `IGitChangesAgentClient` to bypass that.
